              "n": 1,
              "text": "<b>1</b>  to prevent self-pollination / to ensure cross-pollination <b>; </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 2,
              "text": "<b>2 </b> so, must cross with / other parent must be / pollen comes from, a, different / selected, plant / parent / individual / variety <b>;</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 3,
              "text": "<b>3 </b> to make plant a female parent <b>; </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "er": [],
        "aiSupplement": {
          "explanation": [
            {
              "text": "Inbreeding can establish homozygous lines with uniform traits. Crossing different lines produces heterozygous F1 offspring, but their offspring can segregate and lose uniformity.",
              "refs": [
                "syllabus:17.2(7)",
                "ms:b#1"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "reasoningChain": [
            "Distinguish production of parental lines from their final cross.",
            "Explain why the F1 phenotype is not reliably reproduced by saving F2 seed."
          ],
          "inferredMistakes": [
